      {
        "id": 185220,
        "name": "WarrenAC",
        "username": "WarrenAC",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/d2c977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-24T06:23:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"ogseamus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ogseamus/48/4830_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ogseamus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think Rogue Agent really changes KNYFE. You go from straight damage dealing to a choice. Either deal damage or help a hero get set up (mostly).As for all heroes and variants, I am most excited for The Naturalist, Adament Sentinels (I wonder if we will be able to mix with original) and Requital Capt Cosmic. All of them are interesting and fun to play.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>On reddit GTGChristopher said:</p>\n<blockquote><p>You can totally mix and match.\n</p><p>I mean, in my opinion.&nbsp;<em>shrug</em>\n</p></blockquote>\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/sentinelsmultiverse/comments/5472c3/the_sentinels_variants_question/",
        "post_number": 24,
